## @remotion/whisper-web Integration Guide

This document outlines the steps taken to integrate `@remotion/whisper-web` into the frontend application for live audio transcription.

### 1. Installation

First, install the `@remotion/whisper-web` package and ensure all `@remotion/*` packages are updated to the same exact version. This prevents potential version conflicts.

```bash
npm i --save-exact @remotion/whisper-web@4.0.347 remotion@4.0.347 @remotion/cli@4.0.347 @remotion/lambda@4.0.347 @remotion/media-utils@4.0.347 @remotion/paths@4.0.347 @remotion/shapes@4.0.347 @remotion/transitions@4.0.347
```

### 2. Vite Configuration

To use `@remotion/whisper-web` with Vite, two main changes are required in `vite.config.ts`:

1.  **Exclude from Dependency Optimization**: Prevent known issues by excluding `@remotion/whisper-web` from Vite's dependency optimization.
2.  **Configure Cross-Origin Isolation Headers**: Enable `SharedArrayBuffer` support, which is a security requirement for `@remotion/whisper-web`.

`vite.config.ts` modifications:

```typescript
import { defineConfig } from "vite";
import react from "@vitejs/plugin-react";
import path from "path";
import runtimeErrorOverlay from "@replit/vite-plugin-runtime-error-modal";

export default defineConfig({
  optimizeDeps: {
    // turn off dependency optimization: `https://github.com/vitejs/vite/issues/11672#issuecomment-1397855641`
    exclude: ['@remotion/whisper-web'],
  },
  plugins: [
    react(),
    runtimeErrorOverlay(),
    ...(process.env.NODE_ENV !== "production" &&
    process.env.REPL_ID !== undefined
      ? [
          await import("@replit/vite-plugin-cartographer").then((m) =>
            m.cartographer()
          ),
          await import("@replit/vite-plugin-dev-banner").then((m) =>
            m.devBanner()
          ),
        ]
      : []),
  ],
  resolve: {
    alias: {
      "@": path.resolve(import.meta.dirname, "client", "src"),
      "@shared": path.resolve(import.meta.dirname, "shared"),
      "@assets": path.resolve(import.meta.dirname, "attached_assets"),
    },
  },
  root: path.resolve(import.meta.dirname, "client"),
  build: {
    outDir: path.resolve(import.meta.dirname, "dist/public"),
    emptyOutDir: true,
  },
  server: {
    host: "0.0.0.0", // required for external access
    port: 5173, // your vite dev port
    allowedHosts: [
      "1a18e9b5688e.ngrok-free.app", // ✅ allow your ngrok domain
    ],
    headers: {
      'Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy': 'require-corp',
      'Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy': 'same-origin',
    },
    fs: {
      strict: true,
      deny: ["**/.*"],
    },
  },
});
```

### 3. Frontend Integration (RecordingScreen.jsx)

The `@remotion/whisper-web` functionality was integrated into the `RecordingScreen.jsx` component to handle audio recording, model downloading, resampling, and live transcription display.

Key changes in `client/src/pages/RecordingScreen.jsx`:

-   **Imports**: Added `useEffect`, `useRef`, and functions from `@remotion/whisper-web`.
-   **State Management**: Introduced `transcription`, `isTranscribing`, `modelDownloaded` states, and `modelToUse` ref.
-   **Model Download**: A `useEffect` hook handles the asynchronous download of the Whisper model (`tiny.en`) upon component mount.
-   **Audio Processing and Transcription**: Another `useEffect` hook triggers when recording stops and audio chunks are available. It resamples the audio, transcribes it using the downloaded model, and updates the `transcription` state.
-   **Display Transcription**: The transcribed text is displayed on the screen below the recording stats.

```jsx
import { useState, useEffect, useRef } from "react";
import { MicButton } from "../components/MicButton";
import { WaveformVisualizer } from "../components/WaveformVisualizer";
import { useRecording } from "../hooks/useRecording";
import { transcribe, canUseWhisperWeb, resampleTo16Khz, downloadWhisperModel } from '@remotion/whisper-web';

export default function RecordingScreen() {
  const { isRecording, duration, quality, toggleRecording, mediaRecorder, audioChunks } = useRecording();
  const [selectedLanguage] = useState("Hindi");
  const [transcription, setTranscription] = useState("");
  const [isTranscribing, setIsTranscribing] = useState(false);
  const [modelDownloaded, setModelDownloaded] = useState(false);
  const modelToUse = useRef('tiny.en');

  useEffect(() => {
    const setupWhisper = async () => {
      const { supported, detailedReason } = await canUseWhisperWeb(modelToUse.current);
      if (!supported) {
        console.error(`Whisper Web is not supported in this environment: ${detailedReason}`);
        return;
      }

      console.log('Downloading model...');
      await downloadWhisperModel({
        model: modelToUse.current,
        onProgress: ({ progress }) => console.log(`Downloading model (${Math.round(progress * 100)}%)...`),
      });
      setModelDownloaded(true);
      console.log('Model downloaded.');
    };

    setupWhisper();
  }, []);

  useEffect(() => {
    if (!isRecording && audioChunks.length > 0 && modelDownloaded && !isTranscribing) {
      const processAudio = async () => {
        setIsTranscribing(true);
        const audioBlob = new Blob(audioChunks, { type: 'audio/wav' });
        const audioFile = new File([audioBlob], 'audio.wav');

        console.log('Resampling audio...');
        const channelWaveform = await resampleTo16Khz({
          file: audioFile,
          onProgress: (p) => console.log(`Resampling audio (${Math.round(p * 100)}%)...`),
        });

        console.log('Transcribing...');
        const { transcription: newTranscription } = await transcribe({
          channelWaveform,
          model: modelToUse.current,
          onProgress: (p) => console.log(`Transcribing (${Math.round(p * 100)}%)...`),
        });

        setTranscription(newTranscription.map((t) => t.text).join(' '));
        setIsTranscribing(false);
      };
      processAudio();
    }
  }, [isRecording, audioChunks, modelDownloaded, isTranscribing]);

  const formatDuration = (seconds) => {
    const mins = Math.floor(seconds / 60);
    const secs = seconds % 60;
    return `${mins.toString().padStart(2, '0')}:${secs.toString().padStart(2, '0')}`;
  };

  return (
    <div className="text-center space-y-8">
      <h2 className="text-3xl font-bold mb-8">Ready to Record</h2>
      
      <MicButton 
        onRecordingChange={toggleRecording}
        data-testid="main-mic-button"
      />
      
      {/* Audio Waveform Visualization */}
      <WaveformVisualizer 
        isActive={isRecording}
        className="mb-8"
      />
      
      {/* Recording Stats */}
      <div className="grid grid-cols-3 gap-6 max-w-md mx-auto">
        <div className="glassmorphism rounded-xl p-4 text-center" data-testid="duration-display">
          <div className="text-2xl font-bold text-blue-400">{formatDuration(duration)}</div>
          <div className="text-sm text-muted-foreground">Duration</div>
        </div>
        <div className="glassmorphism rounded-xl p-4 text-center" data-testid="quality-display">
          <div className="text-2xl font-bold text-green-400">{quality}%</div>
          <div className="text-sm text-muted-foreground">Quality</div>
        </div>
        <div className="glassmorphism rounded-xl p-4 text-center" data-testid="language-display">
          <div className="text-2xl font-bold text-purple-400">{selectedLanguage}</div>
          <div className="text-sm text-muted-foreground">Language</div>
        </div>
      </div>

      {transcription && (
        <div className="mt-8 p-4 bg-gray-800 rounded-lg text-left">
          <h3 className="text-xl font-bold mb-2">Transcription:</h3>
          <p>{transcription}</p>
        </div>
      )}
    </div>
  );
}
```